abstract: >-
  The Swarm Data Fusion (SwarmDF) toolbox is an open-source Python toolbox for
  analysing the local electrodynamics of the high-latitude ionosphere by combining measurements
  from ESA's Swarm satellites with complementary ionospheric and thermospheric datasets. Given a
  Swarm satellite ID, a regional grid, and a time interval, the toolbox automatically retrieves and
  combines observations from SuperDARN, SuperMAG, Iridium/AMPERE, and Swarm electromagnetic field 
  measurements. SwarmDF uses the local mapping of polar ionospheric electrodynamics (Lompe) technique 
  to reconstruct two-dimensional maps of key electrodynamic parameters along a Swarm satellite trajectory. 
  SwarmDF integrates the LompeOSSE Python module, enabling validation of the Lompe reconstruction against 
  synthetic data generated from Gamera simulations. Featuring an end-to-end automated workflow and a 
  user-friendly graphical interface, SwarmDF simplifies data handling and experiment setup for high-latitude 
  ionospheric electrodynamic studies using Swarm observations.
